,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1593.044029303,"data":"NECESSITY gap (full model[audit] - last-turn-removed[this run]) = +0.0402 macro-F1\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1593.044036029,"data":"SUFFICIENCY gap (full model[audit] - last-turn-only[audit])      = +0.0001 macro-F1  (cited, not re-computed)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1593.044041942,"data":"========================================================================\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1593.044047511,"data":"Reading these two gaps together:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1593.044078291,"data":"  - small SUFFICIENCY gap  -\u003e the closing turn is enough on its own (already known).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1593.044084428,"data":"  - small NECESSITY gap   -\u003e the rest of the dialogue can also fully substitute for\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1593.044090264,"data":"    the closing turn once it's hidden. Both small at once means the label is\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1593.044095964,"data":"    heavily over-determined in this corpus: it leaks from more than one place.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1593.044101686,"data":"  - small SUFFICIENCY gap + LARGE necessity gap is the interesting split-outcome:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1593.04410658,"data":"    the closing turn is sufficient (fast/explicit) but NOT redundant -- hide it and\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1593.044111297,"data":"    the rest of the dialogue is not enough to recover it. That is what a corpus\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1593.044115898,"data":"    with genuine reversals (Arm B / Arm C) is expected to surface.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1593.044120568,"data":"\n"}
